Description: Wild OS ribbon for Write and Tables
 A notebookbar .ui can set wildos-file-label, wildos-file-menu and
 wildos-search-label on an sfxlo-NotebookbarTabControl. The tab control then
 draws the Wild OS ribbon from the design boards instead of native tabs:
 plain tab labels with an accent underline under the current one (no
 100 px minimum), the page as one flat band under the tab row (no tab pane
 frame), a File button in the accent colour before the tabs that opens the
 named popup menu, and a Find a command field at the end of the row where
 the menu button was, which opens the command popup over itself. Each
 group (a prioritised box) is followed by a hairline and group labels are
 drawn in the quiet ink, so the .ui needs no separators.
 Notebookbars without those properties are drawn as before.
 A priority box keeps no room for its >> button while every group fits,
 so a ribbon only folds when it has to.
 A toolbox with wildos-no-arrows set in the .ui keeps drop-down arrows
 and menus off its buttons (Paste and Table on the boards), so a click
 runs the command itself: Paste pastes, Table opens Insert Table.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

